              ],
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "content": "Fig. 9.11: Packed oil"
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "index": 14,
          "bbox": [
            0.115,
            0.684,
            0.467,
            0.705
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "9.5.1 Determination of density"
            }
          ],
          "level": 2
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 15,
          "bbox": [
            0.114,
            0.707,
            0.743,
            0.746
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "The density of an object can be determined by measuring its mass and volume."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "index": 16,
          "bbox": [
            0.115,
            0.757,
            0.383,
            0.776
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "How to measure mass?"
            }
          ],
          "level": 2
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 17,
          "bbox": [
            0.114,
            0.779,
            0.744,
            0.911
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "You learnt the term ‘mass’ in Curiosity, Grade 6. "
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Mass",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " is the quantity of matter present in any object. The instrument used to measure the mass of an object is known as a "
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "balance",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": ". You must have seen various types of balances being used by shopkeepers. Here, we are using a "
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "digital weighing balance",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " to measure the mass. You learnt in chapter ‘Exploring Forces’ that on Earth, weight and mass are closely related."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "footer",
          "index": 18,
          "bbox": [
